  ],
  "notes": [
    "20 mA per I/O pin is the design figure; 40 mA is the absolute maximum and 200 mA is the limit across the whole chip. Drive motors and strips through a transistor or driver.",
    "D13 is wired to the on-board LED through a resistor, so it already has a load. It is a poor choice for an input.",
    "A4/A5 are the only I2C pins. A0-A5 all work as ordinary digital pins (14-19) when you do not need the ADC.",
    "D0/D1 are shared with the USB-serial bridge. Anything attached there fights the serial monitor and the bootloader.",
    "VIN accepts 7-12 V through the barrel jack regulator. Feeding 5 V into the 5V pin bypasses the regulator and its protection.",
    "The R3 and R4 have the same header layout, but the R4 is a 5 V RA4M1 (Minima) or RA4M1 + ESP32-S3 (WiFi) and its peripheral mapping differs."
  ],
